🚀 What is an Endpoint in AWS SageMaker?

An Endpoint is a deployed machine learning model that can receive data and return a prediction.

(The endpoint acts like the connection point between your application and the deployed ML model)

====

Simple flow
Train ML Model 🧠
       ↓
Deploy Model 🚀
       ↓
Create Endpoint 🌐
       ↓
Your Website/App sends data
       ↓
Endpoint processes it
       ↓
Prediction / Response

====

Example: House Price Prediction 🏠

Your model is trained to predict house prices.

Website
   ↓
Send: 2 BHK, Chennai, 1200 sq.ft
   ↓
SageMaker Endpoint
   ↓
ML Model 🧠
   ↓
Return: ₹65,00,000

So:

Model 🧠 = The trained AI/ML brain
Endpoint 🚪 = The access point/API to communicate with that model
Application 🌐 = Sends requests to the endpoint

===

Easy analogy
Restaurant 🍽️
Customer → Waiter → Kitchen

AI Application → Endpoint → ML Model

The endpoint acts like the connection point between your application and the deployed ML model.

In SageMaker, after creating a model, you typically deploy it to an endpoint so applications can make real-time predictions.

